-- Milestone 1, step 5 (companion pet collection): migrate every remaining
-- stock companion pet to the same learn-once/summon-forever pattern Black
-- Tabby piloted (20261004120000_world.sql). See /ARCHITECTURE.md.
--
-- Scope: every item_template row whose on-use spell is
-- SPELL_EFFECT_SUMMON_CRITTER (97), resolved through the server's own
-- progressive-patch logic (item_template.patch against the live WowPatch
-- config = 10, spell_template.build against SUPPORTED_CLIENT_BUILD = 5875)
-- rather than taken at face value - the DB carries historical pre-1.12
-- revisions and later-build stubs (TBC+ era pet rows) under the same entries,
-- and only the row each selector actually resolves to is what a real 1.12.1
-- character can obtain. Generated programmatically from a live-DB query, not
-- hand-typed - verified before applying: every item row's diff against its
-- original is exactly {spellid_1, spellcharges_1} and nothing else, same
-- discipline as the pilot migration.
--
-- 64 new Summon spells (SPELL_EFFECT_SUMMON_CRITTER, same creature/visual/
-- icon as the stock spell each item already used) and 69 new Teach spells
-- (SPELL_EFFECT_LEARN_SPELL, one per item - the six Moro'gai Gem colors all
-- teach the one shared "Ar'lia" Summon spell, matching how they already all
-- pointed at the same stock spell 22567 before this). IDs 60003-60135,
-- continuing straight on from the pilot's 60001/60002.
--
-- `equippedItemClass` is -1 on every new spell (the actual bug fixed live on
-- the pilot - see that migration's own note - caught here before it shipped,
-- not after).
--
-- Two name collisions in the source data, both resolved by hand rather than
-- left to the generator's default "strip the leading Summon " rule:
--   - The six Moro'gai Gem colors (Red/Blue/Green/Black/Gold/White) share
--     spell 22567 "Summon Ar'lia" - one shared Summon spell, six Teach
--     spells (one per gem), not six duplicate pets.
--   - Item 18597 "Orcish Orphan Whistle" and 18598 "Human Orphan Whistle"
--     both use a stock spell literally named "Summon Orphan" (two different
--     spell ids, 23012 and 23013, teaching two different creatures) - named
--     "Orcish Orphan"/"Human Orphan" here instead of colliding on "Orphan".


DELETE FROM `item_template` WHERE (`entry`=4401 AND `patch`=0)
   OR (`entry`=8485 AND `patch`=0)
